===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|skór}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*skōhaz}}, of unclear etymology; possibly a derivation from {{m|gem-pro|*skehaną||to move quickly}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*skek-||to move quickly, jump}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/skouːr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ouːr|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|skós|skór}}

# {{lb|is|footwear}} a [[shoe]]

====Declension====
{{rfinfl|is|noun}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|skóhorn}}
* {{l|is|vera bundinn í báða skó}} (to [[have one's hands tied]])
* {{l|is|gera skóna}} (''governs dative''; to assume something)
*: ''Það má '''gera''' því '''skóna'''.''
*:: It can be '''assumed'''.

